+// Archipelago, natively: the multiworld client inside Savage Wind. Options > Archipelago (game_options.mm) holds the
+// server, slot, password and links (settings.h ap_*); Connect starts this. One thread reads the websocket (WinHTTP:
+// TLS for wss:// with nothing to ship), one does the game side twice a second while Link is in the world:
+//  - checks: each missing location's game data flag (id - LOC_BASE = the flag's crc32; runtime/gdt_flags.c) going on
+//  - items: what the room's slot data "actions" says for each (give / givekey: runtime/items.c; !set / !add / !addf: a
+//    game data flag; !trap: weather or the hour; !demo n: the game's own item-get scene, see demo(); "@k <action>":
+//    only for the k-th copy of the item), from a count kept per room in <data>/ap/
+//  - the goal: Calamity Ganon defeated with the champion powers (and Master Sword) the slot data asks for
+//  - DeathLink (runtime/assists.c), TrapLink, RingLink (the CurrentRupee flag)
+// Notifications are drawn at the bottom left of the game (ap_overlay_draw, from menu.mm's frame); Enter in the world
+// opens the chat there: the room's log to scroll, and a line to talk or ask for a !hint (a Say packet).
+#include <math.h>
